  "presentation_summary": [
    "24-year-old woman with asthma and GERD presented after an upper respiratory tract infection with severe central pleuritic/positional chest pain, chest tightness, shortness of breath, cough, high fever, and neck/shoulder myalgias.",
    "Vital signs included initial heart rate 105/min, temperature 103.3 F, respiratory rate 18/min, and oxygen saturation 99% on room air.",
    "Labs showed positive ANA, anti-RNP >8.0 AI, anti-Sm >8.0 AI, anti-dsDNA 12 IU/L, anti-SS >0.2 AI, CK 3744 U/L, myoglobin >500 ng/mL, CRP 13.20 mg/dL, ESR 86 mm/hr, WBC 10.6 K/mm3, hemoglobin 11.7 g/dL, sodium 126.1 mEq/L, AST 185 U/L, ALT 86 U/L, and albumin 2.7 g/dL.",
    "Chest CT/CTA showed mild left pleural effusion, small pericardial effusion, and bilateral lower-lobe interstitial infiltrates without pulmonary embolism; echocardiography showed small pericardial effusion and EF 65-70%.",
    "Treatment response and paper diagnosis are retained but not used as diagnosis labels."
  ],
